-- title:
--   Local degree of ι(s) bounded by v_{R_h}(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, and let $Pl$ be a valuation subring of an algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ of $\mathbf Q$ such that $p$, viewed in $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, lies in the set of nonunits of $Pl$ (this is the predicate `LiesOverPrime`, unfolded). Let $R_h$ be a commutative domain which is a henselian local ring and a discrete valuation ring, equipped with an algebra structure over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ whose structure map is injective (faithful scalar action), and assume: the image of every $x \in R_h$ lies in $Pl$; an element $x \in R_h$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R_h$ if and only if the $Pl$-valuation of its image is $< 1$; and $R_h$ carries a $\mathbf Z/p$-algebra structure whose structure map sends $x$ to $0$ exactly when the $Pl$-valuation of the image of $x$ is $< 1$. Let $\iota \colon \overline{\mathbf Q} \to \overline{\mathbf Q}_p$ be a ring homomorphism into the algebraic closure of $\mathbf Q_p$ such that $t \in Pl$ if and only if $\|\iota t\| \le 1$. Then for every finite subset $s \subseteq R_h$, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbf Q}_p / \mathbf Q_p$ generated by the image of $s$ under $x \mapsto \iota(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,x)$ is finite-dimensional over $\mathbf Q_p$, and its degree, regarded in $\mathbf N \cup \{\infty\}$, is at most the additive valuation $v_{R_h}(p)$ of $p$ in $R_h$.
--
--   This is the local-degree bound underlying the passage from a henselian discrete valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ with residue field $\mathbf F_p$ to finite extensions of $\mathbf Q_p$: ramification and residue degrees over $\mathbf Q$ are bounded by $v_{R_h}(p)$ and by $[\kappa(R_h):\mathbf F_p]=1$ respectively. It is used to produce, by a union over finite subsets, a single finite-dimensional intermediate field containing the image of $R_h$, in [`ValuationSubring.exists_intermediateField_finiteDimensional_forall_apply_mem_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_of_liesOverPrime`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_intermediateField_finiteDimensional_forall_apply_mem_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_of_liesOverPrime).
